### Secure Ledger API examples
# Works with the IntelliJ HTTP Client and the VS Code REST Client extension.
# Start the stack first (see README). The demo profile loads fictitious accounts with fixed ids.
# Run the requests from top to bottom.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@authUrl = http://localhost:9000
# Client secrets as in your .env (the values of .env.example are already filled in).
@walletSecret = local-dev-only-wallet
@marketplaceSecret = local-dev-only-marketplace
@auditorSecret = local-dev-only-auditor
# Paste the access_token returned by the token requests below; do not commit real tokens.
@walletToken =
@auditorToken =
@marketplaceToken =
# Fictitious demo accounts: Ana and Bruno belong to demo-wallet, the third one to demo-marketplace.
@ana = a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
@bruno = a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002
@marketplaceAccount = b2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
# Paste the id of a transaction returned below to read or reverse it.
@transactionId =
# Use a fresh value for every new operation; repeat it only to retry the same operation.
@transferKey = 7f3c2a10-5b8e-4d21-9c6f-1e2d3c4b5a60

### Token of demo-wallet (scopes ledger.read and ledger.operate)
POST {{authUrl}}/oauth2/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&scope=ledger.read%20ledger.operate&client_id=demo-wallet&client_secret={{walletSecret}}

### Read-only token of demo-wallet: writes with it answer 403
POST {{authUrl}}/oauth2/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&scope=ledger.read&client_id=demo-wallet&client_secret={{walletSecret}}

### Token of demo-auditor (scope ledger.audit: whole audit trail and reconciliation)
POST {{authUrl}}/oauth2/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&scope=ledger.audit&client_id=demo-auditor&client_secret={{auditorSecret}}

### Token of demo-marketplace, another client
POST {{authUrl}}/oauth2/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&scope=ledger.read%20ledger.operate&client_id=demo-marketplace&client_secret={{marketplaceSecret}}

### Accounts of demo-wallet with their balances
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{walletToken}}

### Transfer 150.00 from Ana to Bruno
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{walletToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{transferKey}}

{
  "sourceAccountId": "{{ana}}",
  "destinationAccountId": "{{bruno}}",
  "amount": "150.00",
  "currency": "BRL",
  "reference": "Divisao do aluguel"
}

### Retry with the same key and body: same response, Idempotent-Replayed: true, no second movement
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{walletToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{transferKey}}

{
  "sourceAccountId": "{{ana}}",
  "destinationAccountId": "{{bruno}}",
  "amount": "150.00",
  "currency": "BRL",
  "reference": "Divisao do aluguel"
}

### Same key with another amount: 422 idempotency-key-reused
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{walletToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{transferKey}}

{
  "sourceAccountId": "{{ana}}",
  "destinationAccountId": "{{bruno}}",
  "amount": "151.00",
  "currency": "BRL"
}

### Audit trail of demo-wallet: SUCCEEDED, REPLAYED and REJECTED for the same key
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit-events?limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{walletToken}}

### Withdrawal beyond the balance: 422 insufficient-funds, nothing moves
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/withdrawals
Authorization: Bearer {{walletToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: 2b9d4e61-0c7a-4f38-8e15-6a3b2c1d0e94

{
  "accountId": "{{bruno}}",
  "amount": "100000.00",
  "currency": "BRL"
}

### Deposit into Bruno's account
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{walletToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: 9a1e5c3b-7d2f-4b60-a8c4-3f0e1d2c5b77

{
  "accountId": "{{bruno}}",
  "amount": "35.50",
  "currency": "BRL",
  "reference": "Recarga ficticia"
}

### Statement of Ana, newest first; pass nextCursor back as ?cursor= for older entries
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/accounts/{{ana}}/entries?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{walletToken}}

### Statement of a period as CSV (oldest first); adjust the dates to include today
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/accounts/{{ana}}/statement.csv?from=2026-01-01T00:00:00Z&to=2027-01-01T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{walletToken}}

### A transaction with its entries
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transactions/{{transactionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{walletToken}}

### Reverse it: posts the opposite entries; a second reversal answers 409 already-reversed
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transactions/{{transactionId}}/reversal
Authorization: Bearer {{walletToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: 4c8f2a17-3e6b-4d95-b0a2-7e1f9c3d5a28

{
  "reference": "Lancado em duplicidade"
}

### demo-wallet cannot see the account of demo-marketplace: 404, as if it did not exist
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/accounts/{{marketplaceAccount}}
Authorization: Bearer {{walletToken}}

### demo-marketplace sees its own account
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/accounts/{{marketplaceAccount}}
Authorization: Bearer {{marketplaceToken}}

### Back office: every client's audit events
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/audit-events?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{auditorToken}}

### Back office: reconcile balances and transactions against the entries
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/reconciliations
Authorization: Bearer {{auditorToken}}

### Health and metrics (no token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/prometheus
